{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Ms. ___ . I'm Dr. ___ , one of your oncology team members. You're here today for your eighth cycle of high-dose methotrexate for your lymphoma. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’m doing okay. No new symptoms. Just the usual back pain, but it’s manageable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. We reviewed your labs from this morning. Your white blood cell count is a bit low at 2.0, but stable. We’ll monitor it closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that because of the last treatment? I remember getting neutropenic before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, chemotherapy can lower your white counts. But you’ve tolerated it well so far. We’ll give you the methotrexate today at the reduced dose of 3500 mg per square meter to help avoid mucositis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds familiar. Last time I had mouth sores, but it wasn’t as bad as the first dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re keeping the lower dose to help prevent that. The infusion will start soon, and we’ll begin leucovorin rescue 24 hours later to protect your healthy cells."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll stay here until the methotrexate level drops below 0.05, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s correct. We’ll check your levels daily. Once it’s below 0.05 and you’re stable, you can go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. What about my diabetes? I stopped metformin during the last admission."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re checking your blood sugar four times a day and with insulin as needed. You’ll restart metformin when you go home, but at a higher dose—500 mg in the morning and 1000 mg at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, so it’s being increased? I thought we were being cautious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your sugars have been well-controlled, and your kidney function is good. The team feels it’s safe to increase it now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, I trust you. And my back pain—I’m still on methadone, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll continue your regular methadone. We’ve also added cyclobenzaprine and oxycodone for breakthrough pain if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2152-04-16 11:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ve been using the oxycodone occasionally at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2152-04-16 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve started your methotrexate infusion. It will run over several hours. The nurse will check on you regularly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2152-04-16 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. No nausea or dizziness so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2152-04-17 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How did you sleep? The infusion finished yesterday without issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2152-04-17 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Pretty well. Back was stiff, but I took some oxycodone. Any side effects yet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2152-04-17 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of mucositis or nausea so far—great news. We’ve started your leucovorin this morning to help clear the methotrexate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2152-04-17 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. When will we know about my blood counts?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2152-04-17 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll have updated labs tomorrow. We expect your white count to drop further—that’s expected with this treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2152-04-17 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And that’s why I need to avoid crowds and sick people after I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2152-04-17 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll also prescribe ciprofloxacin to help prevent infection while your counts are low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2152-04-17 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. It’s just for a week, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2152-04-17 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, seven days. We’ll send it home with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2152-04-18 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your methotrexate level is now 0.03, which is excellent. It means your body is clearing the drug well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2152-04-18 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s below 0.05—great! Does that mean I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2152-04-18 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge tomorrow. Your white count is low—0.6—but you have no fever or infection, so it’s safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2152-04-18 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My energy is a bit low, but I feel okay overall."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2152-04-18 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common. Your body is recovering. We’ll make sure you have enough support at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2152-04-18 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have home health coming. What about my potassium? My levels were low last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2152-04-18 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your potassium is low today at 3.0. We’re starting a new supplement—two 20 mEq tablets daily. That’s 40 mEq total."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2152-04-18 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll take those with meals. And I’m still on the IVIG every three weeks?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2152-04-18 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and you received your inhaled pentamidine yesterday for PCP prevention, as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2152-04-18 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t want to get sick from that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2152-04-18 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve updated your discharge meds. Leucovorin will be 20 mg every six hours for two more days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2152-04-18 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s four 5 mg tablets every six hours?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2152-04-18 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And ciprofloxacin twice a day for a week. We’ll send prescriptions with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2152-04-18 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Any changes to my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2152-04-18 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Mirtazapine is now 15 mg at bedtime instead of 30. We’re tapering it to reduce drowsiness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2152-04-18 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have been feeling groggy in the mornings. That might help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2152-04-18 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We hope so. Duloxetine and pregabalin are now both at bedtime to simplify your schedule."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2152-04-18 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s easier. I sometimes forget the duloxetine during the day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared for discharge. Your methotrexate level is safe, and you’re stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What’s the plan for follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have labs checked soon. The oncology team will review your MRI results to decide whether the next treatment will be more methotrexate or R-CHOP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope the tumor is shrinking. I’ve come a long way."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You really have. You’ve tolerated this well, and that’s a big win. Keep taking your meds, avoid illness, and call if you develop fever or mouth sores."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate all your care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you soon for follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to take the leucovorin on time and watch for any nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and use ondansetron if needed. You have it prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the cipro—I take that with or without food?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "With food to avoid stomach upset. Twice a day for seven days, even if you feel fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Understood. I’ll set reminders."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. The nurse will go over your discharge instructions one more time before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I feel ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad you’re doing well. Rest, stay hydrated, and take it easy for a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the best plan. We’re here for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—my ostomy. Any concerns?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No issues noted. Keep monitoring output and stay hydrated. Call if you see major changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you at your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2152-04-19 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2152-04-16 10:33:00",
    "admission_end": "2152-04-19 16:44:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for her eighth cycle of high-dose methotrexate for diffuse large B-cell lymphoma with CNS involvement. She tolerated the chemotherapy well, with no signs of mucositis or infection. Methotrexate was administered at a reduced dose of 3500 mg/m² and followed by leucovorin rescue. Her methotrexate level declined to 0.03, allowing discharge. She remained neutropenic with an ANC of 420 but was afebrile and stable. Diabetes management included holding metformin during admission and increasing the dose upon discharge. Potassium supplementation was initiated due to hypokalemia. Prophylactic ciprofloxacin was prescribed for neutropenia. The patient was discharged home with instructions to continue leucovorin, monitor for infection, and follow up for lab testing and oncology evaluation.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Other malignant lymphomas, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Common variable immunodeficiency",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Lumbago",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Colostomy status",
      "Neutropenia, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
